## UI Stack

Fill in once the first UI-touching slice records the canonical paths,
view/controller layout, and app configuration files.

## UI Principles

- Preserve UI patterns already established in the app.
- Optimize for clear operational workflows over decorative layouts.
- Keep interaction flows discoverable, restartable, and role-aware.
- Accessibility checks are part of normal verification, not polish work.

## Guardrails

- Do not hard-code user-visible copy when an i18n key should be used.
- Keep route, target, model, and service changes synchronized with the app manifest.
- When changing a UI action, inspect the controller, view, fragment, formatter, utility code, and i18n keys together.
- Preserve existing role and visibility checks unless the product/security spec changes them.
- Record key user-facing states: empty, loading, success, error, retry.
- Avoid broad UI rewrites; make scoped changes in the existing structure.

## Verification Expectations

- For controller/view changes, run the relevant baseline build and a local UI start path when feasible.
- Capture browser/runtime evidence for critical user journeys in the relevant plan.
- If visual regressions are common in a flow, standardize screenshot or DOM checks in the plan.
